{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["And he shall appoint overseers, etc., and one fifth — that the officials shall collect a fifth of all produce for the king's needs, whereas the law in other years is a tithe, as written in Samuel: ״את שדותיכם יעשר״ — now he takes a double portion; and similarly Yosef ultimately instituted upon the land of Egypt for Pharaoh — a fifth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The lemma quotes only the opening words 'ויפקד פקידים וגו׳ וחמש'; the fuller phrase 'על אדמת מצרים לפרעה לחומש' at the end echoes Genesis 47:24 and may be read as part of the lemma or as Rashbam's own concluding clause."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:58.467374118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}